  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#26296\", \"PowerToys#44821\", \"PowerToys#33575\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before. Mouse Without Borders currently runs only between Windows PCs. There is no Android, iPad or iOS support. The main tracking ticket is PowerToys#26296, and PowerToys#33575 was closed as a duplicate of it. Please add a thumbs-up to #26296 instead of opening a new request. The ticket also says Linux and iPad were mentioned for the same idea. Phone screen sharing is a different feature from sharing a keyboard and mouse, and it is not part of Mouse Without Borders. Until something like that exists, the tickets suggest scrcpy (https://github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy). It mirrors and controls an Android phone from your PC. Phone Link is another option, though one commenter says it may only work on some Samsung phones.\"}",
